  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "XState in plain words",
      "items": [
        "Actor: a worker with its own state that talks only by sending messages, called events",
        "State machine: an actor's named states and the moves allowed between them",
        "spawnChild: a parent actor starts a child actor; here, one per graph node",
        "sendParent / sendTo: send an event such as NODE.ACK to another actor",
        "invoke + fromPromise: run an async function as a short-lived actor that reports done or error",
        "Final state: the actor has finished, so its parent can stop it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Start (1–3)",
      "items": [
        "1 runGraph creates the root actor from the graphLogic machine, starts it, and waits for its output",
        "2 The root picks ready nodes with plan() and saves that plan to the checkpoint file first",
        "3 It starts one child actor for the node and tells it NODE.ADMITTED"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Run the agent (4–7)",
      "items": [
        "4 The node actor enters its spawning state and invokes an async task",
        "5–6 The task asks the host and manager to run the subagent in a child Pi session",
        "7 The result returns through the host and the task; the task's done event (onDone) hands it to the node actor, which checks it against outputSchema"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Save and clean up (8–14)",
      "items": [
        "8 The node asks the root to record its result (NODE.REQUEST, operation settle)",
        "9–10 The root saves the result, then confirms with NODE.ACK",
        "11–13 Release handshake: ready to stop, you may stop, stopped (final state)",
        "14 The root stops the child and plans the next node; when all nodes are done, its output resolves runGraph"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why save before replying?",
      "items": [
        "The root writes a checkpoint before it admits a node (2) and before it confirms a result (10), so a restarted session resumes from the file",
        "NODE.ACK repeats the whole request, so it cannot approve a different operation",
        "A child counts against the run's parallel limit until the root stops it after NODE.RELEASED"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Beyond this example",
      "items": [
        "decision_gate nodes use the same node machine; their async task calls the decider chain instead of a subagent",
        "expand, fanout, bounded_feedback and graph nodes run coordinator actors that use COORD.* events; a graph node runs a nested root machine",
        "On cancel or failure the root sends CANCEL or FAIL; a failed child reports NODE.DRAINED",
        "XState only runs the graph: the graph definition is plain data, and checkpoints, not XState snapshots, persist",
        "An opt-in XState inspection log records actor ids, events and states"
      ]
    }
  ],
